{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d37324d7-1bd1-4ce8-93b2-333162273eb9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-914aa264e8aea4d5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-2q4wt9il/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Console idle and stale resource reports with CSV export\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the idle resource reporting capability in the RHOAI web\nconsole: a per-project idle-workbench report and a stale pipeline-run report,\nplus CSV export of either report. Cluster administrators get a single place in\nthe console to see which resources are sitting idle — workbenches nobody has\ntouched in weeks that keep their volumes and reservations, and old pipeline\nruns accumulating storage — so they can reclaim capacity with confidence. The\ndata already exists on the platform (the notebook controller tracks\nlast-activity timestamps; Kubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata);\nthis epic surfaces it, it does not build new data collection.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console, showing per workbench:\n  - last activity, sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking\n  - owner\n  - reserved resources\n- Stale pipeline-run report in the web console, showing per project:\n  - completed runs older than a configurable age\n  - retained artifacts associated with those runs\n  - sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata\n- The stale-run age threshold is configurable by administrators\n- CSV export of either report (workbench report or pipeline-run report)\n- Reports are read-only views; no reclamation or deletion actions (explicitly\n  out of scope in the strategy)\n\nThe notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines components undergo no code\nchanges in this epic; they are consumed as-is. Demonstrating that the console\ncan read the notebook controller's last-activity data and the Kubeflow\nPipelines run completion metadata is part of this epic's verification.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the\n  idle-workbench report, then it lists each workbench with its last activity\n  (from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner, and reserved\n  resources.\n- Given a project containing pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the\n  stale pipeline-run report with a configured age threshold, then it lists the\n  completed runs older than that age together with their retained artifacts,\n  and the listed runs match the Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given a configured stale-run age threshold, when an administrator changes\n  it, then the stale pipeline-run report reflects the new threshold without\n  requiring a console redeployment.\n- Given either report, when an administrator exports it, then a CSV file is\n  produced containing the same rows and columns as the on-screen report.\n- The reports introduce no reclamation or deletion actions (read-only).\n- The console build and existing test suite pass with the new reports included.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report — covered by this epic.\n- HLR-3 (P2): CSV export of either report — covered by this epic. Bundled with\n  the P1 report work rather than split: the export acts on the same report UI\n  surfaces and data structures, so it is not independently deferrable and\n  splitting it would force a second pass over the same report views.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":27986,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a360368239a34758","agent_id":"a0585e899d3f8df0c","session_id":"0ac6dbf8-8647-4b18-86ad-04e38ef35119","uuid":"9d646775-3a66-45fb-8247-f97f27c0cff2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11: