{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-939c2789-0574-43c8-8055-7d34d3e74aaa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-be17385c3eae39f8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-2q4wt9il/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E002.md","content":"# Document the idle/stale resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the documentation for the console's idle resource reporting\ncapability: product documentation that explains the idle-workbench report and\nthe stale pipeline-run report (what each column means, where the data comes\nfrom, and how to configure the stale-run age threshold) and walks\nadministrators through safe reclamation steps — how to act on the reports to\nreclaim capacity without disrupting active work. The documentation is authored\nafter the console reports exist, against what was actually implemented.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline (topics to author within this epic):\n\n- A doc topic introducing idle resource reporting in the RHOAI web console:\n  what the reports are for and who they are for (cluster administrators)\n- Reference documentation for the per-project idle-workbench report: columns\n  (last activity, owner, reserved resources) and the notebook controller\n  activity data it is sourced from\n- Reference documentation for the stale pipeline-run report: columns, the\n  configurable age threshold (how to view and change it), and the Kubeflow\n  Pipelines run metadata it is sourced from\n- Reference documentation for CSV export of either report\n- A procedural topic on safe reclamation: how an administrator uses the\n  reports to identify idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs and the safe\n  manual steps to reclaim the underlying volumes, reservations, and artifact\n  storage — including what to check before deleting (recent activity, run\n  ownership) and what is intentionally not automated\n- Explicit statement of the boundaries: automated reclamation/deletion and\n  cost/chargeback calculations are not part of the feature\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Published documentation explains both reports (idle-workbench and stale\n  pipeline-run), including every column each report displays and where its\n  data comes from.\n- Published documentation explains how to configure the stale-run age\n  threshold and how to export either report as CSV.\n- Published documentation provides step-by-step safe reclamation guidance for\n  idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs, including pre-deletion checks.\n- Published documentation has been technically reviewed against the\n  implemented console reports (reviewed by or with the implementing team) so\n  that every documented behavior matches the shipped feature.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps —\n  covered by this epic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":28868,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a360368239a34758","agent_id":"a0585e899d3f8df0c","session_id":"0ac6dbf8-8647-4b18-86ad-04e38ef35119","uuid":"389e19f7-d6ce-4254-a6ae-0869d0e51838","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:17:38.309Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
