{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3a09bd1773d10f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstrat_id: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\tscore: 13\n4\tpass: true\n5\trecommendation: accept\n6\tissues:\n7\t- severity: minor\n8\t  criterion: AI Implementability Scoring\n9\t  description: 'E002 scores human_process_gates: 0 while its rationale states no exceptional\n10\t    human approval gate is required beyond ordinary editorial review — the same condition\n11\t    E001 scores +1 for (ordinary PR review only). Re-score the two epics against a\n12\t    consistent standard; per E002 own rationale text the value should be +1.'\n13\terror: null\n14\t---\n15\t# Decomposition Review — RHAISTRAT-9016\n16\t\n17\t## Review Summary\n18\t\n19\tScore: 13/14 — pass\n20\tRecommendation: accept\n21\t\n22\tContract validator: OK (`validate_decomposition.py` exited 0 — epic body sections,\n23\tcanonical component names, Rule 11 docs-last coverage, priority inheritance, and\n24\timplementation-type parallelism all pass). Triage consistency: `triage: null`\n25\t(full decomposition) with 2 epics is expected, not a violation. The Step 0\n26\t\"multiple distinct work streams\" escape (code implementation + substantive\n27\tdocumentation authoring) legitimately applies: HLR-4 calls for new doc topics,\n28\tnot an incidental touch-up.\n29\t\n30\t## Criterion Details\n31\t\n32\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n33\tAll four HLRs map to epics: HLR-1, HLR-2, HLR-3 → E001; HLR-4 → E002. The HLR\n34\tTraceability Matrix is present and complete. HLR-3 (P2, CSV export) is bundled\n35\tinto E001 with an inline rationale in the matrix row — correct per the\n36\tshared-surface exception: the export acts on the same report UI surfaces and\n37\tdata structures the P1 HLRs build, so it is not independently deferrable.\n38\tPriority inheritance: E001 blocks no P0 work (no P0 HLRs exist); E002's P2\n39\tfollows the docs-authoring exception (strategy `priority: Normal` → P2), which\n40\tis correctly applied and does not push priority upstream. No priority collapse\n41\twith deferrable features.\n42\t\n43\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n44\tSingle edge E001 → E002, justified by Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all\n45\tImplementation epics). Diagram uses `graph TD` with the arrow drawn from\n46\tdependency to dependent, matching E002's frontmatter `dependencies:\n47\t[RHAISTRAT-9016-E001]`; E001 has no dependencies, matching the diagram. No\n48\tcircular dependencies, no invalid edges, no konflux/license-validation epics so\n49\tno parallelism rules are in play. Critical path length 2 is appropriate for a\n50\tsmall strategy with a docs-authoring tail. Cross-check of epic content found no\n51\tundocumented data/artifact dependencies: E001 consumes existing notebook\n52\tcontroller and KFP data surfaces (passive components, no epics), and E002's\n53\tconsumption of E001's output is captured by the existing edge. No branch files\n54\texist, and none are needed (no bounded-outcome unknowns).\n55\t\n56\t### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n57\tE001: Dashboard / RHOAI Dashboard, single component and team. E002:\n58\tDocumentation / RHOAI Documentation, single component and team. Both components\n59\tare in the canonical `.context/rhai-components.txt` list. Work-product types are\n60\tcorrectly separated — code implementation (E001) and documentation authoring\n61\t(E002) are distinct epics per the work-product boundary rule. E001 bundles the\n62\ttwo reports (HLR-1/HLR-2) plus CSV export as one logical change over the same\n63\tconsole surface, with the non-split rationale recorded in the DAG Justification\n64\t— this is the Rule 2 same-component/same-team shape, not a heterogeneous\n65\tmonolith, and plausibly fits within the ~2-week guideline. No scope duplication\n66\tacross siblings. The docs team assignment assumption is recorded as a Health\n67\tWarning rather than silently asserted.\n68\t\n69\t### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n70\tNo Investigation epics — justified: the strategy's Open Questions section is\n71\t\"None\", and the one implicit unknown (console consumability of activity/run\n72\tmetadata) is asserted by the strategy and corroborated by the architecture\n73\tcontext (verified: notebooks.md documents per-kernel activity tracking;\n74\tdata-science-pipelines.md documents the KFP v2 REST API; dashboard.md documents\n75\tthat the Dashboard reads CRs and owns no data plane). Residual access details\n76\tare fix-and-retry implementation work, correctly captured as E001 acceptance\n77\tcriteria rather than a gate. Both epics are Implementation and produce concrete\n78\tartifacts. `gated_by`/`gate_failure_impact` are null everywhere, consistent with\n79\tno gates. E001's null `implementation_type` is valid (optional field for a\n80\tgeneral implementation epic).\n81\t\n82\t### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\n83\tBoth epics carry `ai_signals` (correct field for Implementation type) with\n84\trationale files present. E001's values check out against the strategy and\n85\t`.context`: `architecture_claims: 1` cites notebooks.md, data-science-pipelines.md,\n86\tand dashboard.md — all three citations verified accurate against the actual\n87\tcontext files. E002's `architecture_claims: 0` is rubric-correct (no\n88\tarchitecture-context file covers the Documentation component). One arguable\n89\tvalue: E002 scores `human_process_gates: 0` while its own rationale states no\n90\texceptional human approval gate is required beyond ordinary editorial review —\n91\tthe same condition E001 scores +1 for (\"no human approval steps beyond ordinary\n92\tPR review\"). The two epics apply different standards to equivalent conditions;\n93\tone of the two is miscalibrated (by E002's own rationale text, the value should\n94\tbe +1). Flagged as minor with the correction to re-score consistently.\n95\t\n96\t### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n97\tBoth epics have testable, Given/When/Then-style acceptance criteria derived from\n98\tthe HLRs. Rule-mandated ACs: Rule 24 (docs technically reviewed against\n99\timplementation) is present in E002; Rules 23/25 do not apply (no capability\n100\treplacement, no konflux chain). No AC states an externally-controlled\n101\tprecondition — every AC conditions on what the epic itself builds or verifies.\n102\tNo epic body references sibling epics by draft ID.\n103\t\n104\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n105\tAll strategy scope is covered: both reports with their columns and data\n106\tsources, the configurable age threshold, CSV export, and the documentation with\n107\tsafe reclamation steps. The strategy's out-of-scope boundaries (no automated\n108\treclamation, no chargeback) are carried into both epics rather than dropped.\n109\tStrategy-level context is handled well: the missing Impacted Teams /\n110\tDependencies / AC / NFR sections are recorded as Health Warnings, and the\n111\tresource-aggregation risk (Dashboard owns no data plane) is flagged as a\n112\tnon-blocking scope note. No conditional branches are needed (no bounded\n113\toutcomes). The docs-authoring epic exists as required by HLR-4.\n114\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9116319660c8171c","agent_id":"ae654e27aec543d43","session_id":"0ac6dbf8-8647-4b18-86ad-04e38ef35119","uuid":"81406a58-83a2-43cd-8c3a-d1cbb8b6bd43","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:21:32.068Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3a09bd1773d10f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
