{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb6b636613b8c563","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Console idle and stale resource reports with CSV export\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 8\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Console idle and stale resource reports with CSV export\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the idle resource reporting capability in the RHOAI web\n34\tconsole: a per-project idle-workbench report and a stale pipeline-run report,\n35\tplus CSV export of either report. Cluster administrators get a single place in\n36\tthe console to see which resources are sitting idle — workbenches nobody has\n37\ttouched in weeks that keep their volumes and reservations, and old pipeline\n38\truns accumulating storage — so they can reclaim capacity with confidence. The\n39\tdata already exists on the platform (the notebook controller tracks\n40\tlast-activity timestamps; Kubeflow Pipelines retains run completion metadata);\n41\tthis epic surfaces it, it does not build new data collection.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console, showing per workbench:\n46\t  - last activity, sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking\n47\t  - owner\n48\t  - reserved resources\n49\t- Stale pipeline-run report in the web console, showing per project:\n50\t  - completed runs older than a configurable age\n51\t  - retained artifacts associated with those runs\n52\t  - sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata\n53\t- The stale-run age threshold is configurable by administrators\n54\t- CSV export of either report (workbench report or pipeline-run report)\n55\t- Reports are read-only views; no reclamation or deletion actions (explicitly\n56\t  out of scope in the strategy)\n57\t\n58\tThe notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines components undergo no code\n59\tchanges in this epic; they are consumed as-is. Demonstrating that the console\n60\tcan read the notebook controller's last-activity data and the Kubeflow\n61\tPipelines run completion metadata is part of this epic's verification.\n62\t\n63\t## Acceptance Criteria\n64\t\n65\t- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the\n66\t  idle-workbench report, then it lists each workbench with its last activity\n67\t  (from the notebook controller's activity tracking), owner, and reserved\n68\t  resources.\n69\t- Given a project containing pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the\n70\t  stale pipeline-run report with a configured age threshold, then it lists the\n71\t  completed runs older than that age together with their retained artifacts,\n72\t  and the listed runs match the Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n73\t- Given a configured stale-run age threshold, when an administrator changes\n74\t  it, then the stale pipeline-run report reflects the new threshold without\n75\t  requiring a console redeployment.\n76\t- Given either report, when an administrator exports it, then a CSV file is\n77\t  produced containing the same rows and columns as the on-screen report.\n78\t- The reports introduce no reclamation or deletion actions (read-only).\n79\t- The console build and existing test suite pass with the new reports included.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report — covered by this epic.\n84\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report — covered by this epic.\n85\t- HLR-3 (P2): CSV export of either report — covered by this epic. Bundled with\n86\t  the P1 report work rather than split: the export acts on the same report UI\n87\t  surfaces and data structures, so it is not independently deferrable and\n88\t  splitting it would force a second pass over the same report views.\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ccc104752fc6395","agent_id":"a49c5fc41a4b0b96f","session_id":"0ac6dbf8-8647-4b18-86ad-04e38ef35119","uuid":"e0747e64-2467-4f8d-ac33-f9a55d9547ac","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:22:44.679Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb6b636613b8c563","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
